# CRM connection (slot-booking-service).
# Every confirmed booking and every call marked as done is also sent to the InterviewCall CRM.
# Add these to the server's settings file (production: /opt/ic-booking/settings.env), then restart the service.
#
# Before switching it on:
#   1. Run the migration:   npm run migrate        (production image: npm run migrate:prod)   -> creates crm_outbox
#   2. In the CRM, as an admin: Intake monitor > Source keys > system "VSL · slot booking" > Create. The key is shown once.
#      (A different key from the form service's: each service has its own, so one can be revoked on its own.)
#
# While CRM_SYNC_ENABLED is not "true" nothing is queued and nothing is sent: the service behaves exactly as before.
# If the CRM is down or slow, bookings are not affected: events wait in crm_outbox and are retried (30s, 2m, 10m, then every 30m).
# The message needs the person's name and email, which this service reads from the form service when it sends.
CRM_SYNC_ENABLED=true
# The CRM API, including /api/v1 (no trailing slash needed)
CRM_BASE_URL=https://crm.example.com/api/v1
CRM_INTAKE_KEY=ick_replace_with_the_key_from_the_crm
# Optional (defaults shown)
# CRM_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# CRM_POLL_MS=15000

# Bookings made before this was switched on can be sent once, after the service is running with the settings above:
#   npm run crm:backfill -- --since=2026-10-01          (production image: node dist/scripts/crmBackfill.js --since=2026-10-01)
# Safe to repeat: events have fixed ids and the CRM ignores ones it already has.
